From: mscOS <noreply@mscos.local>
Subject: [PATCH] ALSA: usb-audio: mscOS native DSD for CM6632A 64-bit raw subslot (ML No585)

The Mark Levinson No585/No585.5 (0ecb:18a7, C-Media CM6632A) offers a raw-DSD
altsetting with an 8-byte subslot that the generic DSD_RAW path cannot drive.
Expose it as stereo DSD_U32_LE at twice the device clock, program the clock at
half the ALSA rate, keep packets to whole device frames and swap the middle
words of every 16 bytes (L0 R0 L1 R1 -> L0 L1 R0 R1). Wire format read from
C-Media's macOS driver (CmediaUSBDSD.kext 2.7.16, PrepareDoPContent).
The DSD altsetting (EP 0x05) is joined to the PCM device of the same
interface, so one ALSA device offers PCM and native DSD.
All logic in mscos_dsd.c; hooks are one line each. mscos_dsd=0 disables it.

---
